+/* A frame number of a model's animation (D155). PAL's models hold 5/6 of
+ * US's frames at any timing, so on the PAL disc the port takes PAL's number
+ * with US timing too ("PAL 60"), where RT() gave US's: a frame past the
+ * animation's end, or a test the animation never reached. The port's only:
+ * the matching builds keep RT() at these sites, the same constant. */
+#define RF(us, pal) RV(us, pal, us)
+
 /* Code and data only PAL has (D134): a matching build compiles them for PAL
  * alone, so the US build's SHA-1 doesn't move; the port has them always. */
